{"title":"2024 CSMC Problems/Part B Problem 2 Part B","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1\"><a href=\"#Problem_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_2\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_CSMC_Problems/Part_B_Problem_2\" title=\"2024 CSMC Problems/Part B Problem 2\">Problem 2</a></span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_CSMC_Problems/Part_B_Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=T-1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_CSMC_Problems/Part_B_Problem_2_Part_B&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Suppose that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> are real numbers for which <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/7/0/e70181bd505087747f5a90d44c04d18c87006b1e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x) = x^{2} + mx + p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"159\" height=\"21\" /> has two distinct positive real roots. Prove that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/e/1ae959540bc597ecc349f7bc48dfe34f6de8f2ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g(x) = x^{2} - (m^{2} - 2p)x + p^{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"227\" height=\"21\" /> has two distinct positive real roots.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_CSMC_Problems/Part_B_Problem_2_Part_B&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We can suppose that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/7/0/e70181bd505087747f5a90d44c04d18c87006b1e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x) = x^{2} + mx + p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"159\" height=\"21\" /> has roots <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/7/f37bba504894945c07a32f5496d74299a37aa51c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" />. Using vieta's, this means that:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/c/b7c7017630a5f8487984300058c8305536755f2e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r + s = -m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"96\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/9/f/e9f32ecad2e5b13b0589cc1e1e5fd3e714b79ff7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$rs = p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"52\" height=\"13\" />\n</p><p>This means that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/e/08e62c46169c3693beca855433a69e17b20cdd47.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m^{2} - 2p = (-(r + s))^{2} - 2rs = (r + s)^{2} - 2rs$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"362\" height=\"21\" />, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/a/6/8a6814d90afc7b14e7d67fd399bda0231bea3796.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r^{2} + s^{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"56\" height=\"18\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/a/6ea8c125bc2c5eeff00d67a11659e74681621c7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p^{2} = (rs)^{2} = r^{2} s^{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"138\" height=\"21\" />. Thus:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/4/b/b4b61769498d10fa7fd4c55ff046ff58b0a447cf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g(x) = x^{2} - (r^{2} + s^{2})x + r^{2} s^{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"233\" height=\"21\" />\n</p><p>Using vieta's again, we see this would work when the roots are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/2/fe2824044830deac407616cba3b764d79e50137b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r^{2}$\" width=\"14\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/7/b/f7b59ba357a1b54473c0c4dbe8672bb404f04770.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s^{2}$\" width=\"14\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p><p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/7/f37bba504894945c07a32f5496d74299a37aa51c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> are distinct, positive, and real, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/2/fe2824044830deac407616cba3b764d79e50137b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r^{2}$\" width=\"14\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/7/b/f7b59ba357a1b54473c0c4dbe8672bb404f04770.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s^{2}$\" width=\"14\" height=\"15\" /> must be different in value and must both be positive. Thus, these two roots must also be distinct and positive.\n</p><p>Therefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/9/659a6a2610357101d77dbae8eb9bf0b3100c08fd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"32\" height=\"18\" /> has two distinct positive real roots.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_CSMC_Problems/Part_B_Problem_2_Part_B&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Like in solution 1, we can suppose <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/6/c96dd6ec1dc4ad7520fbdc78fcdbec9edd068d0c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"37\" height=\"20\" /> has roots <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/7/f37bba504894945c07a32f5496d74299a37aa51c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> and say <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/c/b7c7017630a5f8487984300058c8305536755f2e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r + s = -m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"96\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/9/f/e9f32ecad2e5b13b0589cc1e1e5fd3e714b79ff7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$rs = p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"52\" height=\"13\" />.\n</p><p>The problem gives that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/7/f37bba504894945c07a32f5496d74299a37aa51c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> are positive, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/7/317440729faba2b233a3547c42e9baccad52b82d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r + s$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"39\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/8/c889d12451d321614e219737373586e45b71a141.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$rs$\" width=\"16\" height=\"8\" /> must be both positive. This means <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/b/19bf07ceb43df8c7388742c5c1a3667791306791.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p &gt; 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"43\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/f/faff6ed3dfd43ddbdcefe376cb63d2e8c7cff628.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m &lt; 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"48\" height=\"13\" />.\n</p><p>For a quadratic equation to have two distinct positive real roots, its discriminant must be greater than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. This means:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/6/b/e6b0f663b847c6cba2b81ece2238cddf8e26c430.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m^{2} - 4p &gt; 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"99\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>The discriminant of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/9/659a6a2610357101d77dbae8eb9bf0b3100c08fd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"32\" height=\"18\" /> is:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/1/7619521572f0a9434b05f96d2f7de7beccea7060.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(m^{2} - 2p)^{2} - 4p^{2} = m^{4} - 4pm^{2} + 4p^{2} - 4p^{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"343\" height=\"21\" />, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/6/9/f694380289ac185d0f2df0af5bc35ba72db48da1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m^{4} - 4pm^{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"89\" height=\"20\" />.\n</p><p>However, we can realise this is just <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/1/d017431e603a2bdbf3b5e2088a477b54a0954795.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m^{2}(m^{2} - 4p)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"103\" height=\"21\" />. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/b/7/7b7a3eb65f83ee39e780961a08b52ecb7aef7953.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m^{2}$\" width=\"22\" height=\"15\" /> must be positive because it is a real number (since it's just the negative of the sum of two real numbers) and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/1/9/119cd6e6eff4a89ea23788366ff64b3825619d74.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m^{2} - 4p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"66\" height=\"20\" /> is positive from before, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/1/d017431e603a2bdbf3b5e2088a477b54a0954795.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m^{2}(m^{2} - 4p)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"103\" height=\"21\" /> must also be positive.\n</p><p>Therefore, the discriminant of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/9/659a6a2610357101d77dbae8eb9bf0b3100c08fd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"32\" height=\"18\" /> is positive, meaning that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/9/659a6a2610357101d77dbae8eb9bf0b3100c08fd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"32\" height=\"18\" /> has two distinct real roots.\n</p><p>Using vieta's again, we see the roots of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/9/659a6a2610357101d77dbae8eb9bf0b3100c08fd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"32\" height=\"18\" /> sum to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/6/516641b1d49c8e278827c85ae885ba9f271d2963.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m^{2} - 2p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"66\" height=\"20\" /> and multiply to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/b/5ab6025259a9dd6a0fea6fc48a34ef3b4ed8028e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p^{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"18\" height=\"20\" />. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/b/5ab6025259a9dd6a0fea6fc48a34ef3b4ed8028e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p^{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"18\" height=\"20\" /> must be positive since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> is real and not equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, so either both roots must be positive or both roots are negative.\n</p><p>Next, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/a/0/2a018638987f2de2d9f36b01a403e10894b1d77e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m^{2} - 2p = (m^{2} - 4p) + 2p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"208\" height=\"21\" />. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> is positive, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/2/c/72c9925c5c9c964c4a3ab50d7516202c1e614310.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"18\" height=\"15\" /> is also positive and this must be greater than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/1/9/119cd6e6eff4a89ea23788366ff64b3825619d74.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m^{2} - 4p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"66\" height=\"20\" />. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/1/9/119cd6e6eff4a89ea23788366ff64b3825619d74.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m^{2} - 4p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"66\" height=\"20\" /> is positive, so this sum is guaranteed to be positive. However, this can't happen if both roots are negative, meaning that both roots must be positive.\n</p><p>Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/9/659a6a2610357101d77dbae8eb9bf0b3100c08fd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"32\" height=\"18\" /> must also have two distinct positive real roots.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018065758\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.023 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.040 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 215/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 78/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 9570/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    7.203      1 2024_CSMC_Problems/Part_B_Problem_2\n100.00%    7.203      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:37461:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018065758 and revision id 289495. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}